Slightly disturbing, but not unprecedented, no.

The point isn't to make the game unbeatable; the point is to try to add
some variety and some additional challenge to the game.  This _can_ be
done in such a manner so that even the top 1% have to figure a different
solution through for each game, though as you say, you can count on the
top 1% doing so on a consistent basis.

